post-it: Icons don't open
symptoms:
	Desktop icons don't respond
		shows: someone took a screenshot of the desktop and set it as the wallpaper, so every icon on it, My Computer and the Recycle Bin too, is only a picture
	Wallpaper is a picture of the desktop
		shows: the picture has fewer colours than the screen, and Display Properties lists the wallpaper as "prank"
	Icons are in a folder hidden in a corner
		shows: a "New Folder" holds every icon; it is hidden mostly off the screen in the bottom right corner, its name behind the taskbar
software steps:
	Open the folder hidden in the corner
	Drag every icon in it onto the desktop
	Change the wallpaper in Display Properties
